From 2871d8193117e414170caf94642e782c8ce81844 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:32:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/32] diag(nvn): DM_NVN_SUBMIT_LAG holds a submission's
 commit (measured negative for the LEGO HP glyph wall)

A submission's commit is held until n further guest submissions begin, a
blocking guest wait, that frame's present, or a bound: the instrument exists
to test whether the title's UI vertex ring is filled after the draw is
recorded and whether GPU latency hides it. It is not: N=1 and N=3, with the
hold proven effective (11,585/11,700 released by a later submit at N=1,
60.0 fps), leave the glyph-atlas wall bit-identical on the same frames.
A zero-timeout poll releases nothing (that poll is the console's still-busy
path); releasing on it defused the hold on the first poll of every frame.
Includes DM_NVN_STATESCAN. Off by default, bit-identical at 0.
