Subject: [PATCH 09/32] fix(nvn): the vertex / index snapshots are off by
 default: they freeze data the engine fills after recording

Reported on the LEGO HP Years 5-7 game-select transition: the snapshot build added a pink
flash. That is the mechanism in reverse. This engine records a draw and fills the ring the
draw reads afterwards, which a console's GPU latency hides; a copy taken at draw time makes
the stale read deterministic instead of hiding it, and it also defeats the pipeline pacing
that would let the GPU see the fill. Measured before this change: the snapshots changed
neither the glyph wall nor the gameplay artefacts (65.01 -> 65.11 luma on the same screen
change; 155 vs 190 isolated bright rows over two 150 s pairs, i.e. noise).

Both stay available for experiments (DM_NVN_VB_SNAP=1, DM_NVN_IB_SNAP=1) but off. Pipeline
pacing (DM_NVN_PIPE_LAG) stays on: with the snapshots gone the GPU now reads a frame later,
which is the behaviour the engine was written against.
