From 91f993b64721f29fea9449341fec5d6986d85146 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thatSchloesser <sschloesser2@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:37:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/32] diag(nvn): bisect the draw list, and a per-present row
 profile to judge it

DM_NVN_DRAW_RANGE=<min>:<max> keeps only the draws whose index in the guest frame is in
the range and drops the rest; DM_NVN_SKIP_DRAW=<min>:<max> is the mirror (drop that range);
DM_NVN_SKIP_FULLSCREEN=1 drops the small full-screen passes (count <= 6, prim 4 or 5, i.e.
post-process / blit / composite draws). DM_NVN_DRAW_RANGE_FRAMES=<a>-<b> applies any of them
only to those guest frames, so a run can still reach the scene under test; before that
window, and outside it, every draw is submitted. The first drop is logged with the frame
and the draw index, so a filter that does nothing is distinguishable from one that fires.

DM_NVN_REGLUM now also records, per present, the mean |row(y) - row(y-1)| over the region
and 16 band means (columns 6 and 7; columns 1-5 are unchanged). It is computed in the
existing completion handler, which does not wait for the GPU and does not disturb pacing.

Measured on LEGO HP Years 5-7: the filter fires as documented (frame 715, draw index 6
with DM_NVN_DRAW_RANGE=0:5 in frames 600-1200). The row profile over a 150 s run: median
0.40, p95 6.17, max 7.08 luma units, and no frame shows the alternating-band signature that
horizontal scanlines would give -- every high row is a bright scene with a vertical
gradient. So the profile is not yet a detector for this artefact and a bisect still needs a
human yes/no or a labelled frame.
