From: thatSchloesser <sschloesser2@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:54:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 12/32] diag(nvn): measure the present, where the artefact has
 to be

The draw and dispatch filters each removed nothing, and DM_NVN_REGLUM -- which reads the
game's frame texture -- sees no banding in it: over 8,284 windowed presents, luma row
profile median 0.31 (max 7.8, every high row a smooth vertical gradient) and a new chroma
row profile (|row(R-G)|, |row(B-G)|) median 0.04, max 0.64. A torn or mis-bound draw would
have to show in one of those. So the artefact is introduced at or after the present, which
is also why no draw-level change has ever affected it.

Three instruments, all numeric, none writing an image:
* DM_NVN_PRESENTPROF=<file>: per present, renders the present pass into an offscreen
  texture -- the picture the window shows -- and records its mean luma and row profile.
  Compared with DM_NVN_REGLUM's row for the same present, this isolates the present path.
  First measurement: present output carries 2-3x the source's row structure (scan median
  1.17 vs 0.46; up to 15.4 vs 6.8), which resampling would do -- but the sample is
  downscaled to 640x360 and can read a reused src, so it is a lead, not a proof.
* DM_NVN_REGLUM now also records a chroma row profile (column 8): multi-coloured banding
  alternates in hue and can carry identical luma, so a luma profile cannot see it.
* "present geometry: source WxH -> drawable WxH (... 1:1 | resampled)" once per change: a
  source that is not the drawable's size is resampled by the present, and a non-integer
  downscale aliases into exactly the horizontal multi-coloured banding reported.
