Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:20:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/32] diag(nvn): DM_NVN_RINGTRACE -- the thread/frame
 timeline of the UI vertex ring

Off by default; nothing in the renderer's behaviour changes when it is unset.

DM_NVN_RINGTRACE=<file>[#<from>-<to>] writes one line per event on the path that
decides artifact A: the guest's own vertex bind (hle_nvn.c, record time), the same
bind at encode time, the submission and the present, plus, at each present, the
contents of the UI ring blocks and what the write watches saw in the frame that
just ended. Every line carries one monotonic clock (the host's g_t0_ns, shared with
the WATCHD lines), the guest thread handle (thr_cur_handle: one guest thread = one
host pthread), the guest frame, the pass, the stream address, the ring-slot base,
its offset, a 128-bit hash of the first 64 bytes there and the first four words.
The draws it logs are the atlas-sampling ones, identified by the rule ag_is_atlas
states (R8, one level, 2D, >= 2M texels) evaluated on the live MTLTexture, so it
needs no DM_NVN_ATLASGUARD and no shader key.

dm/host/probe.c: dm_watch_dyn(), run-time-armed write watches over several ranges
(DM_PROBE_WATCH is fixed at start-up and covers one). Same mechanism -- the page is
write-protected and every store into it is carried out by the fault handler through
a writable alias -- but per-range aggregates instead of a line per store: first
store's time, guest thread, guest pc, the bytes written and the count, which is what
attributes a 4704-byte UI block fill to a thread. dm_watch_dyn_rearm() re-asserts the
protection every present: the pool's own bookkeeping makes the page writable again
after the first burst and the watch goes deaf otherwise (runs/rt5 vs runs/rt6).

Measured with it (orch/timeline/REPORT.md): the UI block is filled by the guest's
main thread (T=1001, pc=sdk+0x489a78, 294x16B stores per block, every third frame),
while bind, draw, submit and present are all one other thread (T=1005), 7.9-9.3 ms
apart -- with no ordering primitive between the two.
