Subject: [PATCH 16/32] diag(nvn): DM_NVN_GPU_LAG -- a real queue depth (no ms
 bound, the present does not drain it), and what it proves

The submit lag already had a frame-count release, but three things defused it: the
DM_NVN_SUBMIT_LAG_MS backstop, the present committing the frame it presents, and the
guest's own blocking SyncWait on fence-1. DM_NVN_GPU_LAG=n removes the first two and
logs the third: every submission reports the depth it was committed at and its own
commit->gpu_start, and the 300-frame line reports the release counts and the
inflight_at_commit histogram.

Measured on LEGO HP 5-7 (oracle, gameplay window): today's path A 7.07 / B 3.47 per
100 presents (runs/glag0b), depth 1 A 6.60 / B 3.72 (runs/glag1), depth 2 A 8.16 /
B 3.48 (runs/glag2) -- no change, because at depth 2 the guest's fence-1 SyncWait
released 11,999 of 12,000 holds and the achieved depth stayed 1. The GPU already
runs a frame behind the CPU: commit->gpu_start is 0.47 ms from a commit that itself
happens at the next submission's begin.

Off by default: DM_NVN_GPU_LAG unset or 0 is the DM_NVN_SUBMIT_LAG path of 928c8c4.
See orch/fix-land/REPORT.md.
