From 18eb1ed9d52267c19a7a7d4af05c4cfff59ca14e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:18:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/32] diag(nvn): DM_VARRAY -- the UI vertex array's (base,
 capacity, cursor) at every bind, draw, submit and present

Measures, off by default and with three loads per sample (no mtl_addr walk, no hashing, no write
watch, because an instrument that costs what DM_NVN_DRAWSTATE costs removes the artefact instead of
measuring it), the trio the vertex-addr report pins at nro0+0x1176078/0x1176080/0x1176088:

  * at each nvnCommandBufferBindVertexBuffers the guest records (recording thread),
  * at each draw whose stream address falls inside an array (replay thread),
  * at each submission and each present, with a per-frame summary,
  * GROW on a base replacement, ZERO on a cursor that reaches 0, RETREAT on a cursor that drops.

It also inventories every {u32 cap, u64 base, u32 used} struct in nro0's image and looks for the base
of a frame's own stream addresses in every module, which is what showed that the array the static
report pins is never read by a draw: base single-valued over 21,629 samples (21,629 samples, one
value; no GROW anywhere), used identical at submit and at present on all 12,458 presents, and din=0
sin=0 on all 2,678 sampled frames (0 of 878 with any of the 16 streams inside the array). The glyph
streams live in the guest heap (0x386662000.. inside the 512 MB pool at 0x380662000), not in this
array, and no module word is a page-aligned base within 16 MB of them.

Full measurements: orch/vertex-fix/REPORT.md. No guest patch: V1 (no-grow) has no execution to
change, V2 (keep the cursor) overflows 5 MB in ~12 frames at the measured ~430 KB/frame, V3 has no
pair that changes across the record->replay window (d(present-submit) = 0 everywhere).
