From 0417814cadd9bfb4302a8f5a9547fd15bfc67c8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thatSchloesser <sschloesser2@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:15:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/32] nvn: ship the UI republish for LEGO HP 5-7 through the
 game profile

The frame's UI (atlas) draws name pool blocks the guest's 5 MB UI staging array has not
written yet: the flush at nro0+0x1bc9b0 copies the array into the pool at frame begin,
before the frame's emission exists, so every UI draw reads the previous frame's bytes at
that offset (a glyph lattice and a vertex fan, one presented frame each).

uip_draw measures the flush's destination from the guest's own array bytes at each draw
(the block a draw names is flush_base + that object's array offset) and copies the array
over it before the draw is encoded, again at the submission and once more at the present;
every copy is read back through the GPU's own buffer (h_after == h_arr). Modes 1/2/3 =
copy+log per frame / measure only / copy+log every 600th frame; unset or 0 is the host's
behaviour unchanged, with no work in any hook.

Enabled for this title the way the other title quirks are: the profile key `ui_republish`
(game.tsv -> DM_GAME_UI_REPUBLISH, dm/games/game.py) sets the default for
010052A00B5D2000 only, and DM_NVN_UI_REPUBLISH overrides it. The destination is measured
from the guest's own array contents, so it is only meaningful where the UI pool mirrors
that array; another title would get NO BASE (a log line, no write) or, worse, a 64-byte
false match, so the global default stays 0.

Measured with the key on (two 215 s runs, no trace, gameplay presents >= 4500): A 546 -> 12
and 12 episodes, B 303 -> 19 and 18, p50 16.68 ms both, 58,574 and 64,660 verified copies,
nbad=0, no crash. DM_NVN_RINGTRACE_ARRAY: aeq=1 on 3,397 of 3,445 UI draws, aeq=0 on none.

Also adds DM_NVN_UIP_PROBE (off by default): the second 5 MB array's base and cursor, once
per 600 frames, for the residual work.
