From d1cbd80881448cd8aa18fbd0404185f091deaf66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thatSchloesser <sschloesser2@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:50:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/32] nvn: capture the pools at the submit
 (DM_NVN_CAPTURE_SNAP), a range of presents, and build nvn_replay at HEAD

DM_NVN_CAPTURE copied the pool bytes last in a submit's step, after the registry and texture
readbacks: 32.0 s after the submit in LEGO HP 5-7, ~70 guest frames of writes into the same pools,
so a captured block was not the block the GPU fetched. DM_NVN_CAPTURE_SNAP=1 copies every pool
region first, right after mtl_finish and before any readback, and the hashing, the diff and the
compression then run on those copies. The records are copied from the same snapshot, so a frame's
records and its pool bytes are one instant. Measured on the title: pool snapshot 17-99 ms at the
submit, and the replayed frame's pool ends 0 blocks from the live run's ('0 written only live').

DM_NVN_CAPTURE=<first>-<last>[/<stride>]:1:<path> captures every present of a range to its own
<path>.<present>.nvncap (the state a captured present filled is cleared between them), and
DM_NVN_CAPTURE_RAW=1 writes the pool regions uncompressed: 871 MB a file in 1.7 s instead of 33 s.

nvn_replay did not build at HEAD: nvn_mtl.m:10152 and hle_nvn.c:1594 both define a static rt_on()
and nvn_replay.m puts them in one translation unit; the tool now renames hle_nvn.c's for the
include. dm_watch_dyn_* and thr_cur_handle, which nvn_mtl.m's diagnostics reference, are weak
definitions in t_host_stubs.c (nothing watched, no guest thread: honest answers for a tool that
links no host probe or thread layer). t_capture_live.m had the same rt_on collision and is fixed
the same way. All of it is diagnostics, off unless its env var is set.
