From 25a443ff09cd33f44541d7c70f8520b6b4e55840 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thatSchloesser <sschloesser2@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:34:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/32] diag(nvn): DM_NVN_DRAWSTAT -- the presented texture
 read back per present on wallcheck.py's 160x90 grid

The per-present capture (DM_NVN_CAPTURE, 839 MB and 22 s a present with SNAP+RAW)
cannot sample 300 presents in one run (261 GB, and the 22 s freeze changes the
artifact's timing). This reads the same bytes -- level 0 slice 0 of the presented
texture, before the present pass, the source of <capture>.live.png -- into a
6-slot ring of shared buffers queued on the present queue (the REGLUM pattern, no
wait), and writes one TSV row per present: present, frame, w, h, mean, white,
nbrh, bright, sat, bsat, hue8, png.

white/nbrh/mean/bright/sat are wallcheck.py's formulas on the same 12x12 box mean,
verified equal to 4 decimals on three PNGs at once; bsat = (mx-mn>80 and L>150);
hue8 = share of the 8 45-degree hue buckets holding a coloured cell. A present that
trips the lattice test (nbrh>38 and white>0.05) or the burst test gets a PNG
(DM_NVN_DRAWSTAT_PNG), encoded on its own queue; DM_NVN_DRAWSTAT_AT forces one.

Off unless DM_NVN_DRAWSTAT is set. 60.0 fps with it on every present (frame time
p50 16.66 ms, GPU p50 6.8 ms).
