+  `25a443f`, branch `lego-hp57-artifact`; this commit adds only this document on top of `25a443f`).
+* Guest modules: `patched_v131072/main.patched.bin` sha256 `8adb12160a60bf52…`,
+  `patched_v131072/nro0.patched.bin` sha256 `56f3bf4fdbb712f3…`.
+* Profile: `nsp/010052A00B5D2000_build/profile/010052A00B5D2000/game.tsv` — `ui_republish 3` (NOT changed by
+  this commit; the reference run overrode it to 0 on the command line).
+* Save: unchanged; `shasum -a 256 -c orch/replay/save0.sha256` → OK (4 files, e.g. `HP1Slot0`
+  `39a12a32…`, `HP2Slot0` `cdc5231a…`).
+* Route (frame-indexed, `orch/loadtruth/run.sh`):
+  `f1100:Right,f1600:A,f3000:A*26/110,f5900:LUp+LRight~4.6*40/240,f6020:LUp+LLeft~4.6*40/240,f5960:A+LUp+LRight+RRight~0.12*20/480,f6080:A+LUp+LLeft+RLeft~0.12*20/480`
+  — the same route as `orch/truth/REPORT.md`, moving continuously from frame 5900.
+* Run lane: `orch/repro/runlane.sh hold` (mkdir lock + `pgrep -x dmhost` immediately before the exec), one
+  `dmhost` at a time, lock released on every exit path.  Nothing pushed.
+
+## 2. The reference run
+
+`runs/off5k1`, launched 2026-11-17 ~12:52 MST.  The user watched it live and gave the verdict above; at the
+moment the verdict arrived (2026-11-17T19:59:47Z) the run had reached **present 4243, guest frame 13482** —
+that present range (`p.1657 … p.4880`, frames 7202-14500) is the sample the verdict is attached to.
+`runs/off5k1/drawstat-at-commit.tsv` is the TSV as it stood at this commit (3,224 rows).
+
+Present geometry in the reference run: `source 1920x1080 -> drawable 5120x2880 (layer 5120x2880, resampled)`,
+MetalFX spatial scaler 1920x1080 → 5120x2880; screen switched 144 → 120 Hz for 60 fps; present snapshots ring
+4 × 1920x1080.
+
+## 3. What this configuration does NOT do
+
+It does **not** run the republish: `DM_NVN_UI_REPUBLISH=0`.  Whatever improvement the user saw here comes from
+the present path (MetalFX + the 4-deep snapshot ring) and/or the 5120×2880 drawable, not from
+`ui_republish`.  Whether the republish adds anything on top is a separate measurement (`on5k2`, §5).
