+## 4. The drawable question — what actually carries the improvement
+
+**There is no switch that sets the drawable directly.** `front_mac.m` consults only `DM_FULLSCREEN`, `DM_WINDOW`,
+`DM_SCREEN_MATCH`, `DM_PAD_MERGE`, `DM_KBD_PLAYER`, `DM_METAL_HUD`; the drawable is the view's backing store
+(`fitDrawable`), so 5120×2880 exists only through the fullscreen window. `DM_RENDER_SCALE` is the game's 3D view
+scale (0.5–1.0), not the drawable. So the drawable is **not a shippable knob**; the profile's `fullscreen on` is
+the only route to it.
+
+**Holding the present path fixed and varying the drawable (republish OFF, nro0, 60/s, moving):**
+
+| drawable | present path | run | presents | wall /100 | nbrh max |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 5120×2880 | MetalFX + snap 4 | `offC`, `offD` | 5,306 / 5,300 | 1.70 / 1.60 | 39.46 / 39.49 |
+| 2560×1440 | MetalFX + snap 4 | `off2560` | 7,401 | **0.00** | 32.64 |
+
+The small drawable is **cleaner**, so the drawable size is **not** the lever — the opposite of the hypothesis.
+
+**The controlled slice at the fixed 2560×1440 drawable — this is the discriminating experiment:**
+
+| present path | GPU load knob | run | presents | wall /100 | nbrh p90 / max | fan /100 |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| bilinear, **no** snapshot ring | — | `off2` (legacy 148-step, same save/route) | 4,813 | **15.58** | 43.996 / 46.91 | 0.79 |
+| bilinear, **no** ring | **`DM_NVN_PASSGPU_SERIAL=1`** (real GPU serialisation) | `load2560` | 5,920 | **15.00** | 44.08 / **51.09** | 0.34 |
+| bilinear, **ring 4** | — | `off2560snap` | 5,181 | **1.68** | 31.38 / 39.46 | 0.00 |
+| **MetalFX, ring 4** | — | `off2560` | 7,401 | **0.00** | 22.81 / 32.64 | 0.00 |
+
+* **GPU load alone does nothing**: adding real GPU serialisation to the dirty configuration leaves it at 15.00
+  per 100 with `nbrh` up to 51.09 (the lattice is still there, one frame at a time). This is not a throttle effect.
+* **The snapshot ring is the carrier**: 15.58 → 1.68 at the same drawable, and the lattice contrast disappears
+  (`nbrh` max 46.9 → 39.5). The ring copies each present into a host texture of its own, so the guest's next frame
+  can no longer overwrite the texture that is being displayed — a structural fix of the presentation, not a delay.
+* **MetalFX adds the rest** at 2560 (1.68 → 0.00). At 5120 the same path leaves the 1.6–1.7 threshold-edge
+  population (no lattice contrast).
+
+**Verdict for what to ship: the present path (snapshot ring + MetalFX), which the profile already carries.**
+The drawable cannot be shipped as a knob and is not the lever. And because GPU load alone changes nothing, the
+remaining artifacts the user still sees are *not* "the GPU is too fast" — they are the guest-side blit quad
+(`ORCH-CONTEXT.md`, final section) and whatever sits below these thresholds.
