+## 5. STEP 3 — speed in the shipped configuration
+
+* **presents/s: 60.00** (`offC` 12,727 presents / 212.1 s, `offD` 11,540 / 192.3, `onD` 12,742 / 212.4); cadence
+  **dt p50 16.67 ms** (p90 16.75–16.79), i.e. exactly the 60 Hz tick, from `DM_NVN_REGLUM`'s own timestamps.
+* The tick is the host's fixed present pacing: `runs/offC/dmhost.log:99  present tick 60 Hz, interval mode game
+  (original semantics) (game profile present_interval; present interval set by the game 1; window, fixed 60 Hz)`.
+  `DM_PRESENT_HZ=60` was set explicitly in every arm, so no arm depended on the default.
+* The title's own logic rate follows the **presented** frame (`hle_nvn.c:1628-1629`: "some of the game's UI logic
+  counts frames … uncapped gives 4181 SaveIndicatorPanel entries and capped at 60 fps gives 0, which matches the
+  ground truth"). At 60.00 presents/s it runs at 1.00×.
+* The guest's own frame counter runs ahead — **2.19–2.65 frames per present** (131–157 frames/s) — because the
+  display link merges frames the guest submits in between ("old frames dropped by merging", 16k–20k per run). That
+  is this configuration's normal behaviour: the run the user praised (`off5k1`) has the same ratio (2.26), and the
+  user did not call it fast. The "speeding up" run was the uncapped one (~110 presents/s), which cannot happen here.
