+## 6. Headless — operational order, and what it costs
+
+`DM_WINDOW=0` was **not** headless: `front_mac.m:251` tests the variable's presence (`if (!getenv("DM_WINDOW"))`),
+so `DM_WINDOW=0` still creates a 1280×720 window, `makeKeyAndOrderFront` + `activateIgnoringOtherApps:YES`. Every
+run before this point took the user's screen (and the user's deliberate un-fullscreening is what my "DRAWABLE LOST"
+gate kept rejecting).
+
+Now: `orch/finalab/runx_headless.sh` runs `env -u DM_WINDOW` (everything else is `runx.sh`'s: lock, single-host
+guard, kill by pid, log layout). Proof from `runs/headless1` (90 s, no keys past 5900):
+
+```
+runs/headless1/dmhost.log:96   present tick 60 Hz, interval mode game (…; no window, fixed 60 Hz)
+runs/headless1/dmhost.log:613  power up to frame 5100: … (60.0 fps)
+grep -c drawable runs/headless1/dmhost.log            -> 0
+grep -c 'front end: drawable' runs/headless1/dmhost.log -> 0      (no window created)
+runs/headless1/drawstat.tsv                            -> header only, 0 presents
+```
+
+So: **no window, the guest runs and is paced at 60.0 fps — but there are no presents and no `present geometry`.**
+Headless never presents (`nvn_mtl.m:13469`: "headless runs never present"), so the presented-texture judge has
+nothing to read. **The artifact cannot be measured headless with any instrument in this tree.** Every wall number
+in §3/§4 therefore comes from a windowed run made before the order; no further windowed run was made after it.
